+# Domain denylist
+
+Origin: the request "make our short links safer" was clarified with the product owner into a concrete,
+testable rule: refuse to shorten URLs that point at operator-listed domains.
+
+## Configuration (FR-1)
+
+```yaml
+shortener:
+  blocked-domains: [evil.example, phish.test]
+```
+
+Or via environment: `SHORTENER_BLOCKED_DOMAINS=evil.example,phish.test`. Entries are trimmed, lower-cased and
+stripped of a trailing dot at startup. The default list is empty, which preserves previous behaviour.
+
+## Behaviour (FR-2)
+
+`POST /api/v1/links` (and every other creation path, because the check lives in `UrlValidator`) returns `400`
+with the problem detail `Links to this domain are blocked by policy` when the host equals a listed domain or
+is any subdomain of it (`login.evil.example`). Matching is case-insensitive.
+
+## What is not blocked (FR-3)
+
+Matching respects DNS label boundaries: with `evil.example` listed, `notevil.example` and `evil.example.com`
+are allowed. Links created before a domain was listed keep working (no retroactive changes).
+
+## Limitations
+
+- The list is static configuration; changes need a restart.
+- No reputation feeds or DNS-based checks; a denylist only stops domains someone has already reported.
